The Gloaming Codex is a thick book titled the Gloaming. Its cover is a tan leather that feels like rock when tapped, and the book carries a weight that does not match its parts when it is moved, the way magic things do. The pages are filled with a deep red ink; the first of them are alchemical recipes and diagrams. The writing has not been read, though its colour matches a vial of red liquid found in the same room.

The book was the centre of the ritual in [[People/Anthony|Anthony's]] apartment in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Gullet/index|Gullet]]. A dog-eared page near the back shows a stairway climbing to a dark hole, with an angelic figure wrapping its arms around the place the stairway leads.

A piece of [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]] held near the book is pulled down to a glowing spot on that page. Pressing a sliver of the stone to the spot brings a flash and pulls those nearby into the book. Inside is a dark place with no ground to speak of, hung with [[Bestiary/Creatures of the Gloaming Codex|ink]] and other things, where the Feyrock spreads through a living hand and a stairway grows out of the dark, leading both further in and back out.
